preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(high - low, rangeLookback)[1] -- the mean bar range
// over the rangeLookback bars ending ONE BAR AGO, so the signal bar is not in
// its own benchmark. The same indexed-Average idiom BarRangeBelowAverageMultiple
// and LargeOutsideBar use.
//
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808),
// and high - low is a price expression with real history, so this is a FRESH
// loop over price -- not WFSafe_AvgTrueRange's rolling accumulator and not a
// mirrored variable buffer. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
//
// The rule is the NEGATION of an AND, i.e. an OR: the bar is too big to be a
// weak signal bar, OR its body is strong enough to carry it. Two ANDed entry
// panes cannot express that, which is why the composite is carried whole and
// why it is not BarRangeBelowAverageMultiple negated -- that gives only the
// first disjunct and throws away the body escape hatch.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[1 + i] - low[1 + i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
